<title>USA: Farrel workers end strike in Connecticut.</title>
<headline>Farrel workers end strike in Connecticut.</headline>
<dateline>ANSONIA, Conn 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farrel Corp on Thursday said unionized workers at two of its facilities had ended their strike after the company agreed to extend their expired contract.</p>
<p>Farrel said in a statement that the workers returned to their jobs at its Ansonia and Derby, Connecticut, assembly, repair, and warehouse facilities on June 24.</p>
<p>The strike lasted about one week, the company said, adding that it was still negotiating the terms of a new contract with Local 3571 of the United Steelworkers of America.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said last week 46 workers were involved in the strike, representing about 22 percent of the workforce at the two facilities.</p>
